# DrapeAI implementation standards

When implementing or changing **any** code in this repo (`api/`, `app/`, `admin/`, `infra/`), follow project standards. **Source of truth:**

- **[docs/rules/CODING-STANDARDS.md](docs/rules/CODING-STANDARDS.md)** — critical rules
- **[docs/rules/CODING-RULES-HANDBOOK.md](docs/rules/CODING-RULES-HANDBOOK.md)** — day-to-day checklist
- **[docs/rules/AGENTS.md](docs/rules/AGENTS.md)** — architecture invariants
- **[docs/README.md](docs/README.md)** — documentation handbook
- **[docs/instructions/](docs/instructions/)** — task profiles (API, Flutter UI, migration, test, review)

If a standard conflicts with an explicit user request, follow the user and note the deviation.

## Non-negotiable

1. **User ownership** — authenticate via Firebase JWT; SQL always filters by `user_id` for user data.
2. **Parameterized SQL** — never concatenate user input into SQL.
3. **No live secrets in git** — never commit `.env` or API keys; document new vars in `.env.example`.
4. **Async API I/O** — FastAPI handlers stay non-blocking; long work via ARQ.
5. **AI / try-on via services** — use `image_gen_provider` / existing AI services + Settings; do not scatter provider SDKs in routes.
6. **Light theme / no emoji** — Material Icons + `AppColors`; no emoji in UI or logs.
7. **Monolith** — do not add microservices unless explicitly asked.
8. **IDM-VTON NC license** — do not claim commercial rights for IDM-VTON without legal clearance.
9. **Update docs** when behaviour/ops/API changes (`docs/` handbook + deep dives).
10. **Scope** — no unrelated refactors; match local style.

## Language quick rules

| Stack | Do | Don't |
|-------|-----|-------|
| Python | async, Pydantic, `$1` SQL, `logging`, `httpx` | SQL f-strings, sync HTTP in async, log secrets |
| Dart | Riverpod, GoRouter, theme tokens, Dio auth | emoji, ignore errors, hardcode secrets |
| Admin React | Admin API client | Direct DB access |

## Before merge

Auth/ownership covered · tests for touched behaviour · no secrets · docs if needed. Human review for auth, migrations, and try-on spend/licensing.
